          "en": "Under the hood,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 52.35,
          "end": 55.53,
          "en": "it uses another React Native community package,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 55.53,
          "end": 57.821,
          "en": "and it works just like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 57.821,
          "end": 61.74,
          "en": "And it's super easy to set up and use in Expo apps.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 61.74,
          "end": 65.25,
          "en": "You can also use it in non Expo apps though.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 65.25,
          "end": 67.27,
          "en": "As always, you should definitely take a look",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 67.27,
          "end": 69.8,
          "en": "at the configuration options here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 69.8,
          "end": 74.24,
          "en": "and the installation instructions for our Expo managed app.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 74.24,
          "end": 77.13,
          "en": "We just need to run this one command here though.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 77.13,
          "end": 79.44,
          "en": "So again, I'm going to install this package,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 79.44,
          "end": 83.763,
          "en": "this time with Expo install react-native-maps.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 84.81,
          "end": 88.36,
          "en": "This installs this Expo package into our project.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 88.36,
          "end": 91.51,
          "en": "And as before, we can of course also learn how to use it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 91.51,
          "end": 94.75999999999999,
          "en": "here and also in the official documentation",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 94.75999999999999,
          "end": 97.03999999999999,
          "en": "of this third party package,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 97.03999999999999,
          "end": 100.763,
          "en": "which is in the end, just wrapped by Expo, so to say.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 101.77000000000001,
          "end": 104.61,
          "en": "Here, you can learn way more about this package,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 104.61,
          "end": 108.78999999999999,
          "en": "about the installation and the usage of this package.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 108.78999999999999,
          "end": 110.6,
          "en": "So, definitely take a detailed look",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 110.6,
          "end": 112.52000000000001,
          "en": "at this documentation as well",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 112.52000000000001,
          "end": 115.393,
          "en": "if you plan on using maps in your applications.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 116.43,
          "end": 119.61,
          "en": "You also should be aware of the configuration options",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 119.61,
          "end": 122.58,
          "en": "mentioned down there, which become important",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 122.58,
          "end": 125.37,
          "en": "once you start deploying your app,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 125.37,
          "end": 128.22,
          "en": "once you start publishing your to the app stores,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 128.22,
          "end": 131.68,
          "en": "something we will do later in the course as well.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 131.68,
          "end": 134.73,
          "en": "Then, additional configuration might be needed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 134.73,
          "end": 138.2,
          "en": "to make your maps work for both iOS and Android.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 138.2,
          "end": 141.17000000000002,
          "en": "So that is also something to be aware of.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 141.17000000000002,
          "end": 143.69,
          "en": "For development however, we don't need to worry about that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 143.69,
          "end": 146.82,
          "en": "and we can just start using this package.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 146.82,
          "end": 150.6,
          "en": "To use it here in map, in my map screen,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 150.6,
          "end": 154.203,
          "en": "we can return a MapView component here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 155.152,
          "end": 159.12,
          "en": "And MapView is imported from React Native maps like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 159.12,
          "end": 163.7,
          "en": "In addition, I will also import one other named export,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 163.7,
          "end": 167.67000000000002,
          "en": "the marker component, so that I cannot just display a map,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 167.67000000000002,
          "end": 170.81,
          "en": "but also a marker on that map.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 170.81,
          "end": 173.67000000000002,
          "en": "Because the MapView component will render a map,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 173.67000000000002,
          "end": 178.67000000000002,
          "en": "and marker then can be used to place markers on that map.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 178.72,
          "end": 181.42,
          "en": "Now, of course, the map should be configured though.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 181.42,
          "end": 185.81,
          "en": "We wanna tell React Native and this package in the end,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 185.81,
          "end": 189.76,
          "en": "which region of the world should be visible on the map.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 189.76,
          "end": 193.04,
          "en": "And we do pass this information to MapView",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 193.04,
          "end": 196.57,
          "en": "with help of the initialRegion prop.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 196.57,
          "end": 198.96,
          "en": "I don't get auto completion here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 198.96,
          "end": 202.1,
          "en": "but if you take a look at the official documentation,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 202.1,
          "end": 204.81,
          "en": "you'll learn that such a initialRegion prop",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 204.81,
          "end": 207.11,
          "en": "can be set on the MapView",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 207.11,
          "end": 210.1,
          "en": "and this will control which region is visible",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 210.1,
          "end": 212.113,
          "en": "on the map when it's first loaded.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 213.07,
          "end": 215.48,
          "en": "Now, this initial region that is set here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 215.48,
          "end": 219.98,
          "en": "should then be an object with a certain set of properties,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 219.98,
          "end": 222.8,
          "en": "which is not up to you, but defined by this package.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 222.8,
          "end": 225.35,
          "en": "And again, you learn all about that here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 225.35,
          "end": 228.293,
          "en": "if you take a look at the official documentation.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 230.05,
          "end": 233.89,
          "en": "Now here, the object that we have to pass as a region",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 233.89,
          "end": 236.69,
          "en": "to initialRegion is an object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 236.69,
          "end": 240.97,
          "en": "that has a latitude property written like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 240.97,
          "end": 243.873,
          "en": "So just lat, but latitude.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 245.22,
          "end": 247.19,
          "en": "A longitude property.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 247.19,
          "end": 252.19,
          "en": "And then also very important, a latitudeDelta property",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 252.437,
          "end": 256.14300000000003,
          "en": "and a longitudeDelta property.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 257.32,
          "end": 260.88,
          "en": "Latitude and longitude will define the center of the map.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 260.88,
          "end": 264.48,
          "en": "And the deltas will basically define how much content",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 264.48,
          "end": 267.45,
          "en": "besides the center will be visible.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 267.45,
          "end": 272.28,
          "en": "It indirectly sets the zoom level of the map.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 272.28,
          "end": 273.37,
          "en": "Now here for the moment,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 273.37,
          "end": 276.63,
          "en": "I will just set some hard coded coordinates.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 276.63,
          "end": 280.3,
          "en": "For latitude, I'll choose 37.78.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 280.3,
          "end": 285.06,
          "en": "For longitude, I'll set minus 122.43.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 285.06,
          "end": 289.2,
          "en": "And for the deltas, I chose some deltas in advance",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 289.2,
          "end": 291.4,
          "en": "which give me the zoom level I want.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 291.4,
          "end": 296.4,
          "en": "And that would be the numbers 0.0922 for the latitudeDelta,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 296.51,
          "end": 301.207,
          "en": "and 0.0421 for the longitudeDelta.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 301.207,
          "end": 304.13,
          "en": "And this will now render as a nice map",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 304.13,
          "end": 306.986,
          "en": "with this as a starting region.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 306.986,
          "end": 309.73,
          "en": "Now, in order to view this map,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 309.73,
          "end": 313.46,
          "en": "we must make sure that we can reach this screen.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 313.46,
          "end": 316.29,
          "en": "And for this, of course, we can go to app JS,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 316.29,
          "end": 319.92,
          "en": "and register a new screen here in our stack navigator.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 319.92,
          "end": 321.01,
          "en": "Because up to this point,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 321.01,
          "end": 323.623,
          "en": "I haven't registered this map screen yet.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 324.78,
          "end": 327.71,
          "en": "But now I will add a new screen named Map,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 327.71,
          "end": 330.16,
          "en": "and the component at which we point here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 330.16,
          "end": 333.15,
          "en": "is the map component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 333.15,
          "end": 336.743,
          "en": "which we import from the screens map file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 338.23,
          "end": 340.986,
          "en": "So this screen is registered here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 340.986,
          "end": 345.74,
          "en": "The map component is imported from our screens file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 345.74,
          "end": 348.923,
          "en": "Now we just need navigate to that screen.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 350.14,
          "end": 353.78,
          "en": "And that should be done from inside the LocationPicker.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 353.78,
          "end": 355.53,
          "en": "Here in the LocationPicker,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 355.53,
          "end": 358.2,
          "en": "we don't just have to get locationHandler,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 358.2,
          "end": 361.56,
          "en": "we also added this other handler function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 361.56,
          "end": 363.29,
          "en": "the pickOnMapHandler.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 364.15,
          "end": 368.06,
          "en": "And it's that function where the map should be opened.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 368.06,
          "end": 370.21,
          "en": "Now, how do we open this map screen?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 370.21,
          "end": 371.75,
          "en": "As we always do.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 371.75,
          "end": 375.72,
          "en": "We navigate to that screen with help of the functionalities",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 375.72,
          "end": 379.86,
          "en": "provided to us by the React navigation package.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 379.86,
          "end": 382.99,
          "en": "Now, since LocationPicker is not a screen component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 382.99,
          "end": 387.3,
          "en": "we don't get a navigation prop here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 387.3,
          "end": 388.592,
          "en": "That won't work.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 388.592,
          "end": 392.672,
          "en": "But we can use the useNavigation hook, of course.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 392.672,
          "end": 395.472,
          "en": "So here we can call useNavigation,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 395.472,
          "end": 400.472,
          "en": "which must be a imported from @react-navigation/native.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 401.89,
          "end": 404.56,
          "en": "And this will give us a navigation object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 404.56,
          "end": 407.06,
          "en": "which has a navigate method.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 407.06,
          "end": 410.81,
          "en": "So now with that setup in pickOnMapHandler,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 410.81,
          "end": 413.7,
          "en": "we can call navigation.navigate,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 413.7,
          "end": 415.53,
          "en": "and then enter the name of our screen,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 415.53,
          "end": 417.77,
          "en": "which in this case is Map.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 417.77,
          "end": 419.24,
          "en": "And that should be all.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 419.24,
          "end": 422.67,
          "en": "If we save that and force a reload, maybe,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 133,
          "start": 422.67,
